<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarbat Khalsa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sarbat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalsa">Khalsa</a>, &quot;the entire Khalsa&quot;, was the general assembly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> community, which met at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akal-takht">Akal Takht</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a>, usually at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaisakhi">Baisakhi</a> and Diwali, during the 18th century. Leaders of the misls gathered there to settle disputes and plan joint campaigns, and its collective resolutions, gurmatta, were binding on all. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> stopped convening it after 1805.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarbat-khalsa.jpg" alt="Sarbat Khalsa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arorasaab · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GURUDWARA_SRI_AKAL_TAKHT_SAHIB.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
